  "content": {
    "id": "p40-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "The lifetimes of a brand of light bulb are normally distributed with mean 1200 hours and SD 80 hours. Find $P(X < 960\\text{ hours})$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$0.0015$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}z&=\\frac{960-1200}{80}\\\\&=-3\\end{aligned}$$\nBy the empirical rule, approximately $99.7\\%$ of values lie within three standard deviations of the mean. The remaining probability is split equally between the two tails.\n$$\\begin{aligned}P(X<960)&=P(z<-3)\\\\&\\approx\\frac{1-0.997}{2}\\\\&=0.0015\\end{aligned}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 23
  },
